# .dockerignore  [What docker build may see]
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose   Keep everything out of the build context except the four things the image needs
# How       Allow-list: ignore everything, then let back in only config.yaml, conda-lock.yml, src/ and the model file
# Why       .env (keys), data/, other files in models/, logs/, tests/, notebooks/ and wandb/ can never enter the image,
#           including files nobody has thought of yet

# Ignore everything
*

# Let back in only what the image needs
!config.yaml
!conda-lock.yml
!src/
!models/model.joblib

# Inside src/, still drop Python's cache files
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.pyc
